model lh12
  tally 1
  on 2026-10-18
  note "Polish FUS old-age pension for insured persons born after 1948: the calculation base divided by the average further life expectancy, in months, for the age at retirement in completed years and months (art. 26 ust. 1-3), from the GUS table that applies to the application date (ust. 5), or the table in force on the day of reaching 60 or 65 if that is more favourable (ust. 6)."
  note "Each GUS table is a version whose rows govern the applications of 1 April to 31 March after its publication. The examples are those of the ZUS press release of 1 April 2026: a woman of 60 and a man of 65, with capital of 500 and 700 thousand zloty."
  note "Neither the act nor the release states a rounding rule. Axis lh12_mode gives the mode of rounding the monthly pension to the grosz; axis lh12_ok gives how the release's 'ok.' reductions are taken to whole zloty."

source fus "Ustawa z dnia 17 grudnia 1998 r. o emeryturach i rentach z Funduszu Ubezpieczeń Społecznych, art. 26 in the wording of the ustawa z dnia 16 listopada 2016 r. (Dz. U. 2017 poz. 38); read in the tekst jednolity Dz. U. 2025 poz. 1749" at "https://api.sejm.gov.pl/eli/acts/DU/2025/1749/text.pdf"

source gus2022 "Komunikat Prezesa Głównego Urzędu Statystycznego z dnia 28 marca 2022 r. w sprawie tablicy średniego dalszego trwania życia kobiet i mężczyzn, M.P. 2022 poz. 372" at "https://api.sejm.gov.pl/eli/acts/MP/2022/372/text.pdf"

source gus2025 "Komunikat Prezesa Głównego Urzędu Statystycznego z dnia 25 marca 2025 r. w sprawie tablicy średniego dalszego trwania życia kobiet i mężczyzn, M.P. 2025 poz. 279" at "https://api.sejm.gov.pl/eli/acts/MP/2025/279/text.pdf"

source gus2026 "Komunikat Prezesa Głównego Urzędu Statystycznego z dnia 25 marca 2026 r. w sprawie tablicy średniego dalszego trwania życia kobiet i mężczyzn, M.P. 2026 poz. 319" at "https://api.sejm.gov.pl/eli/acts/MP/2026/319/text.pdf"

source modeller "The model's own assumptions, each stated with its reason"

source zus "ZUS, Informacja prasowa, Bydgoszcz, 1 kwietnia 2026 r.: Emerytury są niższe, bo żyjemy dłużej. Od 1 kwietnia obowiązuje nowa tablica dalszego trwania życia" at "https://osieciny.pl/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Emerytury-sa-nizsze-bo-zyjemy-dluzej.-Od-1-kwietnia-obowiazuje-nowa-tablica-dalszego-trwania-zycia.pdf"

axis lh12_mode
  down "the monthly pension truncated to the grosz; no rounding rule is stated"
  half-even "the monthly pension rounded to the nearest grosz, a tie to the even grosz; no rounding rule is stated"
  half-up "the monthly pension rounded to the nearest grosz, a tie away from zero; no rounding rule is stated"

axis lh12_ok
  down "an 'ok.' amount is the difference truncated to whole zloty"
  half-up "an 'ok.' amount is the difference rounded to the nearest whole zloty"

index example = [w60_500, m65_500, w60_700, m65_700]

index months_done = 0..11

index years_old = 30..90

input age_months[e in example]: key months_done

input age_years[e in example]: key years_old

input apply_on[e in example]: date

input capital[e in example]: money PLN
  note "the calculation base of art. 25 ust. 1, given as a round total"

input le[a in years_old, mo in months_done]: num
  note "average further life expectancy for completed years a and completed months mo, common to men and women (art. 26 ust. 2-3)"

input reached_on[e in example]: date
  note "the day the insured reached 60 (a woman) or 65 (a man), art. 26 ust. 6"

def divisor[e in example]: num
  note "a count of months the law divides by, so a plain num (LANGUAGE 3.2)"
  rule base v v_fus = le_apply[e]
  rule reached excepts base v v_fus when le_reached[e] < le_apply[e] = le_reached[e]

def le_apply[e in example]: num at apply_on[e] = le[age_years[e], age_months[e]]

def le_reached[e in example]: num at reached_on[e] = le[age_years[e], age_months[e]]

def pension[e in example]: money PLN
  rule base v v_fus = round(capital[e] / divisor[e], 0.01, lh12_mode)

ask cut_ok: round(pension[e] as if {apply_on[e] = 2026-03-31, reached_on[e] = 2026-03-31} - pension[e], 1, lh12_ok) for e in example

ask div_new: divisor[e] for e in example

ask div_old: divisor[e] as if {apply_on[e] = 2026-03-31, reached_on[e] = 2026-03-31} for e in example

ask inc_2022_2025: le[a, 0] as if {law 2025-04-01} - le[a, 0] as if {law 2022-04-01} for a in [60, 65]

ask inc_2025_2026: le[a, 0] as if {law 2026-04-01} - le[a, 0] as if {law 2025-04-01} for a in [60, 65]

ask le_2022: le[a, 0] for a in [60, 65] with law 2022-04-01

ask le_2025: le[a, 0] for a in [60, 65] with law 2025-04-01

ask le_2026: le[a, 0] for a in [60, 65] with law 2026-04-01

ask pension_new: pension[e] for e in example

ask pension_old: pension[e] as if {apply_on[e] = 2026-03-31, reached_on[e] = 2026-03-31} for e in example

version v_fus
  cite fus
  known 2017-01-05
  note "Law, known from its promulgation (LANGUAGE 4.5): the ustawa z dnia 16 listopada 2016 r., Dz. U. 2017 poz. 38 (published 2017-01-05, in force 2017-10-01), art. 1 pkt 8, gave art. 26 ust. 6 its wording of 60 and 65 years; ust. 6 was added by Dz. U. 2015 poz. 552 (published 2015-04-21). Whether an act between 2018 and 2025 changed art. 24-26 isn't checked. The tekst jednolity Dz. U. 2025 poz. 1749 is the locator (LANGUAGE 5.3): art. 24 ust. 1, art. 25 ust. 1, art. 26 ust. 1-6 (pp. 12-15). The amendments Dz. U. 2026 poz. 26 and poz. 425 don't touch art. 24-26. Art. 26 states no rounding of the pension."

